{"model": "mistral:7b", "case_id": "net_4", "category": "internet", "expected_tool": "internet_tool", "called_tool": null, "tool_call_raw": null, "tool_json_valid": false, "tool_correct": false, "final_text": " To provide information about the latest trends in road safety, I will first query the internal knowledge base (RAG tool) for relevant data. If the information is not sufficient, I will then perform an Internet search (Internet tool) to gather more data.\n\nHere are some of the latest trends in road safety:\n\n1. Autonomous vehicles: The development and implementation of self-driving cars are expected to significantly reduce accidents caused by human error.\n\n2. Intelligent infrastructure: Smart roads equipped with sensors and communication systems can help improve traffic flow, reduce congestion, and enhance safety.\n\n3. Advanced driver-assistance systems (ADAS): Features like lane-keeping assistance, adaptive cruise control, and blind-spot detection are becoming increasingly common in modern vehicles, helping drivers avoid accidents.\n\n4. Road safety education: Programs aimed at educating drivers about safe driving practices, such as speed limits, seatbelt usage, and impaired driving, are essential in reducing accidents.\n\n5. Vulnerable road user protection: Initiatives focused on protecting pedestrians, cyclists, and motorcyclists, such as dedicated lanes and improved infrastructure, are crucial for reducing accidents involving these groups.\n\n6. Data-driven solutions: The use of data analytics and artificial intelligence can help identify patterns and trends in traffic accidents, enabling targeted interventions and improvements in road safety.\n\n7. Enforcement and penalties: Strict enforcement of traffic laws and increased penalties for violations can help deter dangerous driving behaviors and promote safer roads.\n\n8. Infrastructure improvements: Building safer roads, such as those with better lighting, wider lanes, and improved signage, can help reduce the risk of accidents.\n\n9. Connected vehicles: Vehicles equipped with communication systems can share real-time data with each other and with infrastructure, enabling improved traffic management and reduced accidents.\n\n10. Public transportation: Investing in efficient and safe public transportation systems can help reduce the number of private vehicles on the road, thereby reducing accidents.", "latency_s": 7.074071999999433, "error": null, "quality_score": null, "quality_reasoning": "[error al juzgar: 404 Client Error: Not Found for url: http://localhost:11434/api/chat]"}
